// Title: Potential WWlib.DLL Sideloading
// Sigma ID: e2e01011-5910-4267-9c3b-4149ed5479cf
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: X__Junior (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-05-18 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, execution, stealth, T1574.001
// Description: Detects potential DLL sideloading of "wwlib.dll"
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/WhichbufferArda/status/1658829954182774784
//   - https://news.sophos.com/en-us/2022/11/03/family-tree-dll-sideloading-cases-may-be-related/
//   - https://securelist.com/apt-luminousmoth/103332/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/image_load/image_load_side_load_wwlib.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\wwlib.dll" and (not(((InitiatingProcessFolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Microsoft Office\\" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft Office\\") and InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\winword.exe" and (FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Microsoft Office\\" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft Office\\"))))
